Subject: Bluetooth: btcentauri_t6050: use standard synchronous setup

On J716s / 26C5035r, the actual controller rejected both Enhanced Setup
Synchronous Connection (0x043d) attempts with Command Status 0x11 before
any synchronous-completion event or SCO TX/RX. The privacy-filtered HCI
capture retained no audio payload or peer addresses.

Use the existing upstream quirk for this T6050 Centauri controller only.
The HCI core then chooses HCI_OP_SETUP_SYNC_CONN, retaining its normal
CVSD/mSBC parameter selection, status handling and credit accounting.
This does not translate commands, fake successful replies, force a codec,
relax SCO descriptor admission or authorize a controller reset. Legacy
setup and actual microphone audio still require hardware qualification.

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btcentauri_t6050.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btcentauri_t6050.c
@@ -1069,6 +1069,10 @@
 	hdev->post_init = cen_hci_post_init;
 	hdev->reset_dup_filter = cen_hci_reset_dup_filter;
 
+	/* 26C5035r rejects enhanced SCO setup with status 0x11. Use the
+	 * standard setup path; keep codec, status and credit handling in HCI.
+	 */
+	hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_ENHANCED_SETUP_SYNC_CONN);
 	hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_FIXUP_LE_EXT_ADV_REPORT_PHY);
 	SET_HCIDEV_DEV(hdev, &pdev->dev);
 	hci_set_drvdata(hdev, bt);
